{"name":"Canadian Tuxedo","hex":"#579aca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tuxedo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A typically black formal jacket worn by men.","The entire suit complementing and including this jacket."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuxedo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jean jacket","blocks":[{"text":"A denim jacket, also called a jean jacket, jeans jacket or trucker jacket, is a jacket made from denim. Introduced in the United States in the late 19th century, it has been a popular type of casual apparel with both men and women and has been described as an iconic element of American fashion. Though a staple of western wear, the denim jacket has also enjoyed a more general appeal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Riga-12_moped._Fortepan_6735.jpg/330px-Riga-12_moped._Fortepan_6735.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_jacket"},{"title":"Canadians","blocks":[{"text":"Canadians are people identified with the country of Canada. This connection may be residential, legal, historical or cultural. For most Canadians, many of these connections exist and are collectively the source of their being Canadian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadians"},{"title":"Black tie","blocks":[{"text":"Black tie is a half-dress Western dress code for evening events, originating in British and North American conventions for attire in the 19th century. In British English, the dress code is often referred to synecdochically by its principal element for men, the dinner suit or dinner jacket. In American English, the equivalent term tuxedo is common. The dinner suit is a black, midnight blue, or white two- or three-piece suit, distinguished by satin or grosgrain jacket lapels and similar stripes along the outseam of the trousers. It is worn with a white dress shirt with standing or turndown collar and link cuffs, a black bow tie, sometimes an evening waistcoat or a cummerbund, and black patent leather dress shoes or court pumps. Accessories may include a semi-formal homburg, bowler, or boater hat. In Britain, some individuals may rebel from the formal dress code by wearing coloured socks or a bow tie that is not black, such as red. For women, an evening gown or other fashionable evening attire may be worn."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Man_wearing_black_tie.jpg/330px-Man_wearing_black_tie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_tie"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg/500px-Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg/1280px-Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg/500px-Denim_Jacket_%2851079649933%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Levi Strauss Type III jacket","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADenim_Jacket_(51079649933).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Canadian_tuxedo.jpg/500px-Canadian_tuxedo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Canadian_tuxedo.jpg/1280px-Canadian_tuxedo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"h